/* ═══ v2.3.5301: THE SWITCH TABLE (grand plan step 7.1, card T PR 1) ═══
 *
 * Every switch of the game, one row a name: every live flag the worker reads
 * (server/src/liveops.js) and every `?name=` the page reads.  The ONE list of
 * names (the plan's rule 2): the report's `sw` (SHAPES part 5) and the wire
 * table's `flag` column are to read it.  The rules: docs/specs/switch-table.md;
 * the page made from it: docs/SWITCHES.md (`node tools/guards/switches.test.mjs
 * --write`, never by hand); the guard: tools/guards/switches.test.mjs.
 *
 * DATA, NO I/O.  Where each name is READ is never typed here: the scanner
 * finds it (tools/guards/lib/switchScan.mjs) and the page prints it.  A row
 * is judged by a person reading the code at the read; the scanner never
 * writes one.
 *
 * THE COLUMNS (every row has every one; the guard fails a row without):
 *   name      as it is thrown: a live flag's name (`farm`), a page switch
 *             with its `?` (`?guest`, from PR 2), a memory saver by its id
 *             (`sfxcache`: `off_sfxcache` on the worker, `?sfxcache=0` on the
 *             page, one row).
 *   side      `worker`, `page` or `both`.
 *   system    card B's (tools/guards/lib/systems.mjs); a name that fits two
 *             takes the system of the file its read is in.
 *   kind      `switch` (a way of the game turned off or on), `value` (a
 *             number or a word to try: `xp_mult`) or `lever` (a test's or the
 *             owner's tool: `testmode`, `?guest=1`).
 *   born      the tag of the change that made it (the number after `v2.3.`),
 *             from the comment at its read or `git log -S`; `'unknown'` when
 *             neither says (counted, never guessed).
 *   thrown    on the worker the value that throws it (`false` for a lower-case
 *             kill switch, `true` for `disable_*`, `off_*` and a put-away
 *             feature's `true`), or the value's range; on the page its form
 *             (`present`, `=1`, `=0` and the words its read also takes, or a
 *             value).
 *   risk      `logic`, `memory` or `chip` (`none` for a lever): what the old
 *             way guards against.
 *   needs     the names it needs (rule 4: it turns off with them).
 *   fallback  `'no'`, or the trigger that still uses its old way, as names in
 *             a file (`'onWindows, onMac in src/game/lookPaletteChoice.js'`).
 *   off       one sentence: what throwing it turns off, or back on.
 *
 * CAPS.  A cap is a row only where the worker reads it as a flag or a comment
 * promises it as a kill switch (liveops.test §8f, §8g: `storeGear`,
 * `dailyChest`, `whirlWindup`, `broCount` among them).  Any other cap's
 * override is the emergency lever of docs/specs/liveops.md, and stays out.
 *
 * ORDER.  The switches the worker throws for the page (both sides), then
 * the worker by name, then the page by name (card T's PR 2 gave the game's
 * side its rows, PR 3 the drawing side).  A new switch adds its row in its
 * own PR (the guard fails it otherwise).
 */
export const SIDES = Object.freeze(['worker', 'page', 'both']);
export const KINDS = Object.freeze(['switch', 'value', 'lever']);
export const RISKS = Object.freeze(['logic', 'memory', 'chip', 'none']);
export const COLUMNS = Object.freeze(['name', 'side', 'system', 'kind', 'born', 'thrown', 'risk', 'needs', 'fallback', 'off']);

